      A(t) is almost pure 2ω — the bed stress ~|U∞|U∞ works twice a cycle. A₂ = 0.216 0.216 0.223 0.219 dec,
      explaining 81–89% of its variance, peaking +0.104 T_tide (+1.8 h) after peak flow.
      The pivot is a phase lag with height: the 2ω signal climbs at 0.29 mm/s
      (18 m per cycle), so the window spans 0.53 cycles of 2ω. Below ½ a cycle the
      tilt absorbs it; at a full cycle it cannot, and the shape term takes over.
      Lₑ(t) is deliberately not quoted: B is comparable to b, so the instantaneous
      slope crosses zero near slack and −1/(b ln10) has a pole there.

